1. DEFINITIONS

"Software" means the ToggleLogic Free package distributed with this License,
including its source files, documentation, and notices. A future release is
Software only if that release is distributed with this License.

"You" means the individual or legal entity exercising rights under this License.

"Affiliate" means an entity that directly or indirectly Controls, is Controlled
by, or is under common Control with You. "Control" means ownership of more than
50% of the outstanding voting power or beneficial equity interests, or the direct
or indirect power to direct management or policies by ownership, voting agreement,
contract, or otherwise. Customary minority-investor protective rights, a board-
observer right, or a passive minority investment alone do not create Control. A
venture, private-equity, or institutional investor and its other portfolio
companies are not Affiliates solely because of such an investment or right.

"Startup Group" means You and every Affiliate. Threshold calculations are made
for the Startup Group as one consolidated group, without double-counting
intercompany transactions or transfers.

"Cumulative Outside Funding" means the gross amount of cash and fair market
value, when received, of non-cash consideration actually received by the Startup
Group after formation from persons outside the Startup Group through: equity or
equity-linked securities; SAFEs or similar instruments; convertible notes or
other equity-convertible debt; securities crowdfunding; venture debt or other
financing raised primarily to fund growth; and non-refundable grants intended to
finance development or operations. It excludes customer revenue and bona fide
customer prepayments; ordinary-course trade credit; equipment leases and
equipment-specific financing; non-equity-linked working-capital facilities from
regulated financial institutions secured principally by receivables, inventory,
or equipment; tax refunds and refundable tax credits; insurance proceeds;
intercompany transfers; and founder capital contributed before the first sale of
outside equity or equity-linked securities. Funding counts when actually received,
not when announced, signed, committed, or approved. Transaction expenses,
repayment, redemption, repurchase, or cancellation do not reduce it.

"Actual Gross Revenue" means revenue recognized by the Startup Group from all
sources under the accounting method consistently used in its books and financial
statements, before operating expenses, cost of revenue, commissions, model or API
costs, hosting costs, or other deductions. It excludes separately stated sales,
use, value-added, and similar transaction taxes collected for a taxing authority,
and refunds and chargebacks actually issued. It is tested on the last day of each
calendar month for the 12 consecutive calendar months ending on that date. If the
Startup Group has existed for fewer than 12 months, the period begins on its
formation date. Revenue is not annualized or projected. Foreign-currency amounts
must use the reasonable, consistently applied conversion method used in the
Startup Group's financial statements.

"Product" means Your bona fide application, service, platform, device, or managed
offering in which the Software is integrated as a component and that provides
material functionality independent of the Software.

"Threshold Event" occurs on the first date the Startup Group either (a) has
received at least USD $1,000,000 in Cumulative Outside Funding or (b) has at least
USD $1,000,000 in Actual Gross Revenue for a trailing 12-month measurement period.
That date is the "Threshold Date." Announced, committed, projected, pipeline,
booked-but-unrecognized, or forecast amounts do not count. Eligibility does not
revive if revenue later declines, funding is repaid, or the group is reorganized.

"Qualifying Startup" means a Startup Group before its first Threshold Event.

"Acquisition Event" means a merger, consolidation, or similar transaction
resulting in a change of Control; a transfer of more than 50% of voting power or
beneficial equity; a transfer of all or substantially all assets; or a transfer of
the Product or business in which the Software is used.

"Excluded Proprietary Components" means materials that are not Software,
including ToggleLogic Intelligence; the Toggle Registry; proprietary benchmark
data, normalization, weighting, selection, and Dynamic Model Determination
methods; private classifiers; private evaluation or customer evidence;
credentials, keys, access controls, services, documentation, or APIs supplied
only under a separate agreement; and other materials expressly identified as
proprietary and excluded. A compatibility seam, detector, interface name,
configuration field, or public description does not grant access to or rights in
an Excluded Proprietary Component.

2. ACCEPTANCE AND RELEASE STABILITY

By exercising rights under this License, You accept it. Rights for a version You
lawfully receive are perpetual and non-revocable except under Section 11.
Licensor may stop distributing the Software and may license future versions under
different terms, but those actions do not revoke rights already granted for this
version. Licensor has no obligation to provide updates, maintenance, support,
hosted services, future compatibility, or a commercial agreement unless separately
agreed in writing.

3. PERSONAL AND INTERNAL USE GRANT

Subject to Your compliance with this License, Licensor grants You a worldwide,
royalty-free, non-exclusive license to use, copy, execute, display, and modify the
Software for personal use and internal business operations.

4. STARTUP COMMERCIAL USE GRANT

While You are a Qualifying Startup, Licensor additionally grants You the right to:

(a) integrate the Software into a Product;
(b) operate or host the Software as part of a Product;
(c) reproduce and distribute the Software solely as an integrated or subordinate
    part of a Product; and
(d) charge customers for the Product.

No advance approval, registration, or contact is required. A Controlled entity
may exercise this grant only as part of the Startup Group and while it remains
Controlled. You are responsible for its compliance.

5. THRESHOLD NOTICE AND TRANSITION

You must notify Licensor at https://togglelogic.ai/contact/ within 30 days after
the Threshold Date. The notice must state Your legal name, primary domain,
responsible contact, Product name and description, whether funding or revenue
triggered the notice, the Threshold Date, a non-sensitive financial range, and
whether You seek commercial licensing, an Intelligence evaluation, support,
partnership, or a migration discussion.

Beginning on the Threshold Date, the Startup Commercial Use Grant is automatically
replaced by a 180-day "Transition License" permitting the same uses authorized
immediately before the Threshold Event. Timely notice is a condition of the
Transition License, subject to the cure provision in Section 11. Licensor and You
may negotiate a commercial agreement or written extension, but neither is required
to enter one.

If no commercial agreement or written extension is effective at the end of the
Transition License, You must stop accepting new customers for, newly deploying,
or materially expanding external commercial use of the Software. For the next 12
months, You may provide security, compatibility, defect-correction, and migration
updates to customers who received or were contractually committed to receive the
Product before the Transition License ended. The internal-use grant in Section 3
continues.

6. DOWNSTREAM CUSTOMER CONTINUITY

Each customer who lawfully receives the Software as an integrated part of a
Product receives directly from Licensor a limited, non-exclusive, non-transferable
license to run that integrated copy solely as part of the Product. The customer
may not extract, redistribute, sublicense, or offer the Software separately. A
later Threshold Event or termination affecting the Product provider does not
retroactively terminate an innocent customer's right to run a lawfully delivered
copy, but does not authorize new versions or updates delivered after the provider's
rights end.

