10. RECORDS AND VERIFICATION

You must keep reasonable records sufficient to determine threshold eligibility.
No more than once in any 12-month period, Licensor may reasonably request
supporting records under confidentiality, unless Licensor has a reasonable basis
to suspect a material misstatement. You need not publicly disclose funding or
revenue under this License.

11. TERMINATION AND CURE

Licensor may terminate Your rights only for a material breach. Except for an
Excluded Serious Breach, rights terminate only if Licensor gives written notice
describing the breach and You do not cure it within 30 days. For Your first
curable breach, complete cure and practical correction of past noncompliance
retroactively reinstate Your rights. A late Threshold Notice is curable by
providing the required notice and information. A substantially similar breach
repeated within 12 months after cure may terminate without a second cure.

"Excluded Serious Breach" means intentional unauthorized access to an Excluded
Proprietary Component, deliberate circumvention of access controls, knowing
material fraud, or deliberate removal of ownership or license notices.

After final termination, You must stop uses no longer licensed and delete or
return unlicensed copies within 30 days, excluding one archival copy retained
solely for legal and compliance purposes and copies lawfully usable by downstream
customers under Section 6. No deletion is required while a cure, Transition
License, written extension, or customer-continuity period remains effective.

12. ACQUISITIONS AND ASSIGNMENT

An Acquisition Event is not a retroactive breach. At closing, the acquired entity
is combined with the acquirer's controlled group for threshold calculations. If
the combined group has crossed either threshold, closing is the Threshold Date.
You may assign this License in a bona fide Acquisition Event if the successor
assumes it in writing and provides notice within 30 days after closing. Other
assignment or sublicensing requires Licensor's written consent.

